i_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Very Spiritual", "text": "Fascinating Place!  We learned a lot about the Hindu religion and found this place very moving and spiritual.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2011-11-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "57BF96C3BF71CC24F6E59F90025CF2AF", "name": "thundering-pause", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/thundering-pause", "username": "thundering-pause", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-s/02/33/1f/e3/thundering-pause.jpg", "contribution_count": 112, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 33447, "location_name": "Golden", "location_name_detailed": "Golden, Colorado"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2011-11-20", "published_at_date": "2011-11-20"}, {"review_id": 120810322, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r120810322-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Interesting", "text": "Awesome, a place to look and consider life.\n\nDisapointing is the attitude of other tourist who consider this just a play? Taking movies/shots of crying relatives of the person who died.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 3, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2011-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "C7970732CAD2192026BB45F5B409A74F", "name": "Roos1911", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Roos1911", "username": "Roos1911", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/08/17/56/6f/roos1911.jpg", "contribution_count": 64, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 188590, "location_name": "Amsterdam", "location_name_detailed": "Amsterdam, The Netherlands"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2011-11-20", "published_at_date": "2011-11-20"}, {"review_id": 120805984, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r120805984-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Watch out for the Funeral Pyres", "text": "Brill place to go to, watch out for the funeral pyres, they can be a bit ngruesome.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2011-11-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "CFAEB02CF6C0D0463393230CAB932AA1", "name": "Nc L", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/maxandcups", "username": "maxandcups", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f1/42/default-avatar-2020-20.jpg", "contribution_count": 17, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 551673, "location_name": "Exmouth", "location_name_detailed": "Exmouth, United Kingdom"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2011-11-20", "published_at_date": "2011-11-19"}, {"review_id": 120767400, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r120767400-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Not really a tourist attraction...keep your camera in your bag", "text": "Going to Pashupatinath was a fascinating experience but in some ways a bit uncomfortable too.  Statement of the obvious but this is a living (and dying) temple.  As non-Hindus we didn't entirely feel like we were supposed to be there.\n\nBut providing you handle the experience respectfully, we don't think you'll feel like you're in the way.  We had two young kids with us.  They were fine: interested in what was going on and keen to learn about the cremation rites we witnessed.  But some young kids could be freaked out by the sights down at the river.  make sure you are ready to explain to them that, yes, they can see someone's legs poking out of the funeral pyre...", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 2, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2011-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "AED4B98FE7A831B4F47B8445A5360E13", "name": "Monkey-and-Sprite", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Monkey-and-Sprite", "username": "Monkey-and-Sprite", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/07/c4/25/c7/monkey-and-sprite.jpg", "contribution_count": 168, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 186361, "location_name": "Oxford", "location_name_detailed": "Oxford, United Kingdom"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2011-11-18", "published_at_date": "2011-11-18"}, {"review_id": 120758620, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r120758620-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Not for weak stomachs", "text": "We paid 500 rupee's each to get into the site.  A lot of guys around claiming to be guides - site is easy to negotiate alone - don't be fooled into parting with your cash.  If you want photo's with the Sadhus you will need to pay them too.  \nIt may seem odd to go to watch a cremation but this is the way of the world - take the time to chat with the people there and you will come away strangely changed in someway - stand and gawp and you are just another tourist..  The bodies are washed in the river first then dressed in white & orange sheets before being laid on the pyre.  Only Hindu's are allowed in the temple but you can peek in from the door.  Make sure you take some peppermints or sweets with you and visit the old peoples home on the right as you walk down - if you go early in the morning your help will be appreciated too.  This is an extremely interesting site which should be on your itinery.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2011-11-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "86AFFB4644C25B722811B35E1A717755", "name": "rosielamb", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/rosielamb", "username": "rosielamb", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/02/39/3f/d0/rosielamb.jpg", "contribution_count": 393, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 2654088, "location_name": "Ramsden", "location_name_detailed": "Ramsden, United Kingdom"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2011-11-18", "published_at_date": "2011-11-18"}, {"review_id": 120571752, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r120571752-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "cremations", "text": "the archeological site is in my opinion not worth it ...quite dirty and smelly too!!\nwitnessing cremation was a very emotional and educational experience!", "review_tip": null, "rating": 3, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2011-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "E38190287555C8BD94A33AB519BB1F89", "name": "mimie71", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/mimie71", "username": "mimie71", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/de/e7/default-avatar-2020-37.jpg", "contribution_count": 14, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 186402, "location_name": "Birmingham", "location_name_detailed": "Birmingham, United Kingdom"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2011-11-14", "published_at_date": "2011-11-1